{
	"id": "branch-type-merging",
	"text": "To get a better handle on how Effect's types infer, let's use succeed and fail together. To do this, we'll define the classic type-safe division example. safeDivide takes the numerator and the denominator, and then checks to see if we're about to divide by zero. If so, we will fail with DivisionByZero. Otherwise, we'll succeed with the quotient. TypeScript will correctly infer the return type is an Effect that can either succeed with a number or fail with DivisionByZero.",
